@startuml agent-registration
!theme plain
title Registering an agent: the dispatcher creates the OS user and binds it in the broker with a grant chain

participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Dispatcher\n(v0: curator agent-user create)" as D
participant "curator-host-helper\n(root, sudoers: this path only)" as H
participant "Key keeper\n(later)" as K
participant "Broker" as B

O -> D: start a worker: role R, profile dev,\nchild grant G_child (narrowed from my G_orch)
D -> D: check: may O start role R?\nG_child ⊆ delegable(G_orch)?
D -> H: sudo helper  (stdin: helper-op/1 {op: user.create, kind: agent, label: dev-7f3})
H --> D: {username: cur-a-dev-7f3, uid: 612, generation: g-0193}
D -> K: register(612, derivation path)  (later)
K --> D: agent public key (later; v0 uses label:dev-7f3)
D -> B: bind {uid 612, generation g-0193, identity label:dev-7f3,\nprofiles [dev], chain [G_child, G_orch, …, root], expires_at: end of task}
B -> B: peer UID is a configured dispatcher;\nverify chain: signatures, narrowing, expiry, revocation;\nleaf subject = binding identity
B --> D: binding/1
D --> O: run handle
@enduml
